INTENDED USE
------------
Intelligence OS is a general-purpose, self-hosted tool for building a
retrospective, correctable memory of what cameras you operate observed. It is
intended for premises the operator is responsible for, with the knowledge of the
people who enter them.

It is not designed for, and the maintainers do not support, covert surveillance,
tracking specific individuals without a lawful basis, or any deployment a
person's safety depends on. It is retrospective by design and is not a safety
interlock.

Face recognition is disabled by default. Enabling it means processing biometric
data, which carries obligations in most jurisdictions (GDPR Art. 9, the EU AI
Act, the Illinois Biometric Information Privacy Act, and others). Responsibility
for establishing a lawful basis, informing data subjects, and honouring their
rights rests entirely with the party operating the software, not with the
authors. See docs/responsible-use.md.


